# CTRLO-OTHER-PICKERS: the /provider column under Ctrl-O, one key at a time
# (the provider scenario's profile). Named provider-* so the sign-in
# ledger rows the provider scenarios share apply. fx's C-j and C-k reach
# the composer (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116
# @481104fd; :881-893): C-k kills nothing (:479-488), C-j is a new line
# after the argument (:513-521). Down and Escape are the transcript's
# (input_full_transcript_runtime.zig:156-197). Down first, so a move would
# show.
# Last, with no Ctrl-O: Backspace takes the new line back, and Alt-Enter
# (ESC CR, insert_newline in both) puts it in again, so the column's anchor
# follows the caret's row without the screen (projectedAnchorColumn,
# visual_layout.zig:705-713; `alt-enter`).
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
seed provider-settings.json
nomodel
gateway slow-line-turn.json
wait 2.5
type /provider 
wait 0.8
key Down
wait 0.4
snap open
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Down
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap down
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Escape
wait 0.8
snap esc
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-k
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap ck
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-j
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap cj
key BSpace
wait 0.4
snap bspace
key M-Enter
wait 0.6
snap alt-enter
